From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlie <5764343+charlielye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:33:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(world-state): open aztec-wsdb's stores with Init,
 not command-line genesis options

aztec-wsdb no longer takes the genesis on its command line. IpcWorldState.spawn starts it with the data
directory, threads, ring sizes and map sizes, then sends Init with the protocol's tree heights and prefill,
the header generator point and this node's prefilled public data, nullifiers and genesis timestamp. If Init
fails, the process is destroyed and the error rethrown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015HXzMEGRnmFYs5yXRcAWCb

